                "content": "1. Introduction:\nWelcome to Yaro, a social voice chat and voice calling application. By using this app, you agree to abide by the following terms and conditions.\n\n2. User Eligibility:\nYou must be at least 18 years old to use this app. By using this app, you confirm that you meet the eligibility criteria.\n\n3. Use of the App:\n- This app allows you to join public and private voice chat rooms and make voice calls to other users.\n- You agree to use the app only for lawful and respectful communication.\n- Any form of abuse, harassment, or objectionable content is strictly prohibited.\n\n4. Account Responsibility:\n- You are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of your account.\n- You must not share your login credentials with anyone.\n- If you suspect any unauthorized access, please report it through the app support section.\n\n5. Privacy & Data:\n- We value your privacy. Your personal data will be handled securely and used only to improve the app experience.\n- Voice data and chat interactions are not shared publicly or with third parties, unless required by law.\n\n6. Payments & Diamonds:\n- The app may offer in-app purchases like coins or premium features.\n- All purchases are final and non-refundable unless stated otherwise by app store policies.\n\n7. Termination of Account:\n- Yaro reserves the right to suspend or terminate your account if you violate any terms.\n- You may also delete your account anytime from the app's settings.\n\n8. App Content:\n- Some visuals, avatars, or icons may be generated using artificial intelligence (AI).\n- These do not represent real individuals. Any similarity is purely coincidental.\n\n9. Changes to Terms:\nWe may update these terms from time to time. Continued use of the app means you accept the updated terms.\n\n10. Support:\nIf you have questions, concerns, or complaints, please reach out to us from the Support section in the app.\n\nNote: These Terms of Use are a general guideline and do not replace any legal rules under applicable laws, including the Indian Penal Code or IT Act."
